;; The sources index: what the knowledge container reads (dhf/spec/knowledge/
;; sources.feature). Each source's provenance record (the .md beside this file)
;; says in prose what it is evidence for; this index says what a machine needs:
;; the repository, every pin ever cited (a pin is never dropped), and the
;; source's fenced paths.
;;
;; scope-impact/rdm is not a source: it holds today's implementation, and its
;; own history is fenced by dhf/harness/config.edn, :fenced-paths.
;;
;; FENCED PATHS. A source that holds an implementation of what rdm-spec
;; regenerates would hand a coding agent the answer, however clean its room
;; (the event storm's hotspot H14, dhf/storm/2026-10-24-rdm.md). So each
;; source's implementation is fenced like rdm-spec's own: never cited, and
;; removed, in tree and history, from the checkout the clean room carries
;; (dhf/spec/regeneration/fence.feature). Specs, documentation and
;; configuration stay readable.
{:innolitics-rdm
 {:repository "https://github.com/innolitics/rdm"
  :record "innolitics-rdm.md"
  :pins ["f21b508"]
  :fenced ["rdm" "tests" "contrib" "setup.py"]}

 :agent-skills
 {:repository "https://github.com/scope-impact/agent-skills"
  :record "agent-skills.md"
  :pins ["da65901"]
  :fenced []}

